  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1205 PM CDT Mon Aug 10 2026\n\nHeadline heat is here to stay as we encounter an evolving high\npressure ridge aloft that only builds/reinforces its influence\nwith time. Currently the Advisory/Warning stretches thru\nThursday, but with each successive run suppressing pcpn chances\nin the medium range, we could see similar temps/dew points right\non thru the weekend and into next week. Daily highs in the\nlower-mid 90s along with daily dew points in the lower to mid \n70s will create triple digit heat indices. For now, it appears \ncollaborative efforts favor holding a steady-as-she goes \napproach with the headlines, in case intermin convective chances\nbreak the cycle. One such chance is over the back half of the \nweek, when the boundary to the north sags southward just enough\nto pick up our pcpn chances. In particular, a potential MCS-like\ncomplex Wednesday may throw a high canopy over us, as it moves \nin later in the day with its marginal risk svr potential;\nsimilar pattern-action Thursday may provide another small \nwindow of strong/svr storm risk. Otherwise chances taper down \nthereafter, with the upper ridge reinforcing itself even more \nstrongly over the weekend. Given the 6-10 and 8-14 day above \nnormal temp outlooks, the remainder of the month may just stay \nvery summer-like for us with a consecutive days streak of 90F \nor higher max temps potentially materializing into something to\ngame watch.",
